## 9. API Architecture

The Certipedia Explorer client initiates secure lookup queries. In the production transition phase, the endpoints will be structured as follows:

```http
# Perform Certificate Lookups
GET /api/certificates?verify={id}&nationalId={nationalId}

# Admin Actions (Requires JWT Auth)
POST /api/certificates
PUT /api/certificates/:id
DELETE /api/certificates/:id
```

### Verification Payload Example (Response)
```json
{
  "id": "VISO-TR-2026-001245",
  "nationalId": "1023456789",
  "status": "VALID",
  "source": "Arabic",
  "target": "English",
  "issue": "16 Aug 2026",
  "expiry": "16 Aug 2027",
  "name": "Corporate Legal Contract"
}
```

* **Request Validation**: Certificate IDs are parsed to uppercase and stripped of extra whitespaces. National IDs must be validated as 10-digit strings.
* **Error Handling**: API errors (e.g., 404 Certificate Not Found, 401 Unauthorized PIN/ID) return unified messages to protect database vulnerability.

